        "id": 3702829
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-10T13:55:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nice catch, a concurrent domain free can mess things up. I shall do a pkvm_iommu_get_domain() and take a refcount to make sure that it doesn\u0027t disappear while being updated.",
      "parentUuid": "314098e9_a06f3fb8",
      "revId": "e63de4f225fbc857aad8ff57c21faf7d265cd82f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cb32aedb_65beca2e",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/hyp/pv_iommu.c",
        "patchSetId": 77
      },
      "lineNbr": 513,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-10T14:02:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The problem is not just with a concurrent free? The domain already exists, everyone may already find it via pkvm_get_iommu_domain() and start using it at any time, while it is still not fully initialized?\n\nThe first obvious solution that comes to mind is just to pass all these parameters to pkvm_alloc_iommu_domain()?",
      "parentUuid": "d9a6559d_7b1ac4cc",
      "revId": "e63de4f225fbc857aad8ff57c21faf7d265cd82f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a26eb913_5c2ca5c3",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/hyp/pv_iommu.c",
        "patchSetId": 77
      },
      "lineNbr": 513,
      "author": {
        "id": 3702829
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-10T14:10:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e The problem is not just with a concurrent free? The domain already exists, everyone may already find it via pkvm_get_iommu_domain() and start using it at any time, while it is still not fully initialized?\n\nPractically this may never happen as domain alloc happens much before context/pasid entry is allocated. domain is used during context/pasid update and map/unmap operations and these happen only after a domain is succesfully created. I think the host code also makes this assumption.\n\n\u003e The first obvious solution that comes to mind is just to pass all these parameters to pkvm_alloc_iommu_domain()?\n\nThis is fine with me, will do this.",
      "parentUuid": "cb32aedb_65beca2e",
      "revId": "e63de4f225fbc857aad8ff57c21faf7d265cd82f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3fa7b471_73cf83ec",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/hyp/pv_iommu.c",
        "patchSetId": 77
      },
      "lineNbr": 513,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-10T14:14:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Practically this may never happen as domain alloc happens much before context/pasid entry is allocated. domain is used during context/pasid update and map/unmap operations and these happen only after a domain is succesfully created. I think the host code also makes this assumption.\n\nEven if so, we don\u0027t trust the host? While it\u0027s the host that controls _when_ to issue any of these hypercalls (domain alloc/free as well as context/pasid update), on any CPU?",
      "parentUuid": "a26eb913_5c2ca5c3",
      "revId": "e63de4f225fbc857aad8ff57c21faf7d265cd82f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "41998dfd_14f40504",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/hyp/pv_iommu.c",
        "patchSetId": 77
      },
      "lineNbr": 513,
      "author": {
        "id": 3702829
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-10T14:34:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Even if so, we don\u0027t trust the host? While it\u0027s the host that controls when to issue any of these hypercalls (domain alloc/free as well as context/pasid update), on any CPU?\n\nBut from a security perspective, we should be safe I guess. The normal functioning of the system may be at risk, but I think we don\u0027t compromise security. If alloc and context/pasid update or map/unmap happens concurrently, I guess the worst that could  happen is DMA initiated by the device fails. If the page donation and related security check works as intended, it will guarantee that no secrets are leaked. And flushing logic also would not be leaking any secrets if any of the above happens concurrently. Is my understanding correct?\n\nI am fine with fixing it by passing it do alloc_domain, but was thinking loud if its really needed :-). We take similar assumptions at various other places and just makes sure the security guarantees are met.\n\nConcurrent domain alloc/free might mess up pKVMs internal data structures and thats why I thought it should be fixed by taking a refcount.",
      "parentUuid": "3fa7b471_73cf83ec",
      "revId": "e63de4f225fbc857aad8ff57c21faf7d265cd82f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
